'''Bœhmeria''' (bė-mē′ri-ä̤), ''n.'' [NL., after G. R. ''Boehmer'' or ''Böhmer'', a German botanist of the 18th century; cf. G. ''Böhme'', a Bohemian, ''Böhmen'', Bohemia.] A genus of dicotyledonous plants, natural order ''Urticaceæ'', allied to the nettle, but without its stinging hairs. {{smaller|A number}}

